{title: Auld Lang Syne}
{subtitle: Beginner arrangement - longer phrases and a shared ending}
{artist: Robert Burns / traditional Scottish}
{lyricist: Robert Burns}
{composer: Traditional Scottish tune}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 72}
{tag: beginner, Scottish, farewell, three chords}
# Public-domain Scots text: The Poetical Works of Robert Burns (1887).
# All five verses retained in that edition's order. Fresh three-chord accompaniment.
{comment: Strum DDDD}
{comment: Sing "Should" as a pickup. Keep counting through long notes and agree the final stop.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Should [C]auld acquaintance [G7]be forgot,
And [C]never brought to [F]min'?
Should [C]auld acquaintance [G7]be forgot,
And [F]days o' [G7]lang [C]syne?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
For [C]auld lang [G7]syne, my dear,
For [C]auld lang [F]syne,
We'll [C]tak a cup o' [G7]kindness yet,
For [F]auld [G7]lang [C]syne.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
We [C]twa hae run a[G7]bout the braes,
And [C]pu'd the gowans [F]fine,
But [C]we've wander'd mony a [G7]weary foot
Sin [F]auld [G7]lang [C]syne.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
For [C]auld lang [G7]syne, my dear,
For [C]auld lang [F]syne,
We'll [C]tak a cup o' [G7]kindness yet,
For [F]auld [G7]lang [C]syne.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
We [C]twa hae paidl't [G7]i' the burn,
From [C]mornin sun till [F]dine;
But [C]seas between us [G7]braid hae roar'd
Sin [F]auld [G7]lang [C]syne.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
For [C]auld lang [G7]syne, my dear,
For [C]auld lang [F]syne,
We'll [C]tak a cup o' [G7]kindness yet,
For [F]auld [G7]lang [C]syne.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
And [C]here's a hand, my [G7]trusty fiere,
And [C]gie's a hand o' [F]thine;
And [C]we'll tak a right guid [G7]willie-waught,
For [F]auld [G7]lang [C]syne.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
For [C]auld lang [G7]syne, my dear,
For [C]auld lang [F]syne,
We'll [C]tak a cup o' [G7]kindness yet,
For [F]auld [G7]lang [C]syne.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
And [C]surely ye'll be [G7]your pint-stowp,
And [C]surely I'll be [F]mine;
And [C]we'll tak a cup o' [G7]kindness yet
For [F]auld [G7]lang [C]syne.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Final chorus}
For [C]auld lang [G7]syne, my dear,
For [C]auld lang [F]syne,
We'll [C]tak a cup o' [G7]kindness yet,
For [F]auld [G7]lang [C]syne.
{end_of_chorus}
